A way of seeing the river as shared space,

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:28.140
that has nothing to do
with Bangkok or Vientiane,

00:25:28.140 --> 00:25:31.470
and much less to do with Beijing,
and cross river authority

00:25:31.470 --> 00:25:34.903
as ruled more by force of
personality than legal mandate.

00:25:36.100 --> 00:25:40.080
But with changes in the
water, become multiple changes

00:25:40.080 --> 00:25:42.250
at the level of authority as well.

00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:45.640
Rapids if not blasted, can
become submerged at a flood

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:49.680
or turn into full-fledged
islands in an ebb.

00:25:49.680 --> 00:25:51.440
And the fisheries, these
fisheries have been some

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:55.150
of the hardest hit by
recent hydro-power projects.

00:25:55.150 --> 00:25:56.440
When floods ripped through the village,

00:25:56.440 --> 00:25:58.470
the most common casualty
are those net strung

00:25:58.470 --> 00:25:59.900
within the fishing grounds.

00:25:59.900 --> 00:26:01.890
The nets already become prone to tangling

00:26:01.890 --> 00:26:04.610
to become a pale blue mess as
they're torn from the eddies

00:26:04.610 --> 00:26:06.100
in which they float.

00:26:06.100 --> 00:26:07.550
Most often, they end up in the morning

00:26:07.550 --> 00:26:10.080
after the flood stranded
on top of a Boulder,

00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:13.589
with fish too ensnared to be
removed rotting in the sun.

00:26:13.589 --> 00:26:16.150
And of these, most are
swept away in too damaged

00:26:16.150 --> 00:26:16.983
to be recovered.

00:26:16.983 --> 00:26:21.503
This is the most of the
financial damage from a flood.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:27.000
That's of the sites
Bong pointed out to me.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:29.920
Many if not most were devoid of nets.

00:26:29.920 --> 00:26:31.520
Here even nets have been swept away,

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:35.570
or equally as often bone
described the owners as waiting,

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:38.290
before they attempted anymore fishing.

00:26:38.290 --> 00:26:40.110
Some had lost nets, and
were waiting for the money

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:43.040
to replace them, and put them back in.

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:45.320
Others were waiting for
the algae bloom to subside,

00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:47.380
but some were simply
waiting for the instability

00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:48.653
and the river to be over.

00:26:49.740 --> 00:26:51.860
Prices for fishing plus
in the entire system

00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:53.990
of mutual ownership went into freefall.

00:26:53.990 --> 00:26:56.230
And recrimination, sometimes
village against village

00:26:56.230 --> 00:26:57.400
since Lao against Thai,

00:26:57.400 --> 00:26:59.420
and sometimes simply into personal flare

00:26:59.420 --> 00:27:00.620
to even turning violent.

00:27:01.660 --> 00:27:03.760
Some, abandoning net fishing altogether,

00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:06.820
turn towards fishing with
electric charges or bums,

00:27:06.820 --> 00:27:08.880
and the Thai police inspector
at the docks in turn

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:13.670
began patrolling Laotian waters
armed, and drunk at times,

00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:15.210
firing at those he thought were fishing

00:27:15.210 --> 00:27:17.810
using these destructive techniques.

00:27:17.810 --> 00:27:20.080
Fishing, and by the
extension the realm managed

00:27:20.080 --> 00:27:22.290
by local authority is changing.

00:27:22.290 --> 00:27:25.020
The new landscape of
potential is uncertain,

00:27:25.020 --> 00:27:27.500
and only after this new world emerges,

00:27:27.500 --> 00:27:28.823
can decisions be made.

00:27:31.120 --> 00:27:34.460
So, I've talked a little bit about ...

00:27:34.460 --> 00:27:36.010
I'm gonna move forward just a little bit.

00:27:36.010 --> 00:27:38.270
I talked a little bit about
the change and the pulse,

00:27:38.270 --> 00:27:40.570
and the yearly pulse of the river.

00:27:40.570 --> 00:27:44.190
And what I wanna focus on,
is how this pulse marks time.

00:27:44.190 --> 00:27:49.190
And in that, as people
decide when to lay the nets,

00:27:49.650 --> 00:27:51.340
and when to use what
particular techniques,

00:27:51.340 --> 00:27:55.840
they do so based upon a
series of Buddhists festivals,

00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:59.643
which are then linked to the
waters flood and its retreat.

00:28:00.530 --> 00:28:03.030
This also involves planting
crops along the riverbank

00:28:03.030 --> 00:28:07.980
as the water dies down, it
leaves a thick silty deposit

00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:10.700
which is really good for planting
particular kinds of crop.

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:12.671
Now where the water rises and falls,

00:28:12.671 --> 00:28:17.343
against natural cycles, this
becomes a possible to protect.

00:28:18.480 --> 00:28:22.450
So, the new Mekong has a
different time from the old one.

00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:25.410
And with it, what was once
efficacious is no longer.

00:28:25.410 --> 00:28:29.050
If we were to reframe this
statement and theoretical terms,

00:28:29.050 --> 00:28:30.730
the Mekong becoming dammed,

00:28:30.730 --> 00:28:34.310
opens onto a new uncertain
field of potentiality.

00:28:34.310 --> 00:28:36.570
And these rhythms of course,

00:28:36.570 --> 00:28:38.590
originate when the Chinese
controlling the dam

00:28:38.590 --> 00:28:40.570
decides to retain or release water,

00:28:40.570 --> 00:28:44.246
decisions that are on principle
not communicated downstream.

00:28:44.246 --> 00:28:47.970
Without the ability to
communicate with the Chinese then,

00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:49.640
fishermen can only watch the water level

00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:52.600
for indication that the
dam controller has acted.

00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:54.290
They know very well,
the cause of the floods,

00:28:54.290 --> 00:28:57.040
but not whether or not one
is coming, and when it will.

00:28:58.430 --> 00:29:01.180
These are also changes to
popular Buddhist practice.

00:29:01.180 --> 00:29:02.970
During the height of the dry season,

00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:06.580
normally sandy islands
rise up out of the water

00:29:06.580 --> 00:29:07.990
as the waterfalls.

00:29:07.990 --> 00:29:09.200
And all these islands,

00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:12.380
village from the Lao side and
the Thai side come together,

00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:14.010
and make the kind of a festival village

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:16.770
where you can raise
tractors, and drink beer,

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:21.770
and engage in all the profits
that low water fishing has.

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:23.262
But in 2015, a glut of water came through

00:29:23.262 --> 00:29:26.633
and wiped out the village,

00:29:27.830 --> 00:29:29.820
causing tens of thousands of dollars

00:29:29.820 --> 00:29:34.090
worth of damage, and entirely
disrupting the whole cycle

00:29:34.090 --> 00:29:39.090
of the whole process of
celebrations for the boosts near.

00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:44.840
So, patterns of rise and fall,
are one stranded in the way

00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:47.040
that one marks its time,
and then they call them.

00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:50.100
A yearly cyclical calendar
punctuated by Buddhist holidays,

00:29:50.100 --> 00:29:53.140
fishing and farming
practices, the monsoon.

00:29:53.140 --> 00:29:55.510
That dry season when you
build festival villages,

00:29:55.510 --> 00:29:56.760
and Sandy islands emerged

00:29:56.760 --> 00:29:58.950
from that flow coincides
with an abundance of fish,

00:29:58.950 --> 00:30:01.300
and large fish are easy
to catch a low water.

00:30:01.300 --> 00:30:03.810
These in turn fuel, temple donations,

00:30:03.810 --> 00:30:06.440
sacrifices to river
beings, and social events,

00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:09.180
and ritual activity centered
upon mobilizing villages

00:30:09.180 --> 00:30:10.230
own potency.

00:30:10.230 --> 00:30:12.880
And around this time, if
anybody of you have been

00:30:12.880 --> 00:30:16.270
to Isan, I know, there's a
rocket festival where large,

00:30:16.270 --> 00:30:18.960
very phallic rockets are
fired up into the sky,

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:20.383
triggering the monsoon.

00:30:21.490 --> 00:30:23.310
So, in this way rituals kind of gain

00:30:23.310 --> 00:30:24.830
the power to yield rain.

00:30:24.830 --> 00:30:27.410
When the waters is near
its height and converse,

00:30:27.410 --> 00:30:29.290
other beings to turn act.

00:30:29.290 --> 00:30:31.560
This is the time when
people see Naga fireballs.

00:30:31.560 --> 00:30:34.800
As Nagas come up, and spit
their own fire into the sky,

00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:38.123
then causing the clouds to
disperse, and the water to drop.

00:30:38.980 --> 00:30:42.230
So, land beings act to break
about the rise of the water,

00:30:42.230 --> 00:30:44.220
river beings act to bring about its ebb.

00:30:44.220 --> 00:30:47.220
The water, that based calendar
that the Mekong mobilizes

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:49.293
the potency of particular technologies.

00:30:50.510 --> 00:30:54.600
So, the dam then alters
time, along the Mekong.

00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:57.510
Monsoon time and Buddhist
time become disrupted

00:30:57.510 --> 00:31:01.650
via new modes of time when the
gates open, when they shut.

00:31:01.650 --> 00:31:03.730
And the wake of the dam, the
river, and those within it

00:31:03.730 --> 00:31:06.150
become disentangled from the rhythms.

00:31:06.150 --> 00:31:08.320
The Mekong water levels no
longer linked to the rain,

00:31:08.320 --> 00:31:11.000
which in turn is delinked
to the ritual activity

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:12.570
meant to provoke rain.

00:31:12.570 --> 00:31:16.490
Fish follow suit, and as the
Naga show, so do river beings.

00:31:16.490 --> 00:31:18.370
So now in the wake of the new Mekong,

00:31:18.370 --> 00:31:21.800
the situated knowledge fails
and new practices arise.

00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:23.940
Moratoriums on fishing
in particular seasons,

00:31:23.940 --> 00:31:25.550
and in particular sites have elapsed,

00:31:25.550 --> 00:31:27.500
and response to falling yield fishermen,

00:31:27.500 --> 00:31:28.970
to compensate for the lack of knowledge,

00:31:28.970 --> 00:31:30.520
how to handle this new river,

00:31:30.520 --> 00:31:32.773
turn towards other fishing techniques.

00:31:34.130 --> 00:31:36.800
As fishermen who no longer trap
fish with old mesh methods,

00:31:36.800 --> 00:31:39.170
and as Naga fireballs
will they still appear,

00:31:39.170 --> 00:31:41.080
do to not bring about a
lowering of the water.

00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:43.860
And as high water comes with,
or without Felic rockets,

00:31:43.860 --> 00:31:46.170
river time is becomes disentangled.

00:31:46.170 --> 00:31:48.570
Disentangled from Buddhist
time, monsoon time,

00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:49.670
calendar time.

00:31:49.670 --> 00:31:51.810
Events that will previously simultaneous,

00:31:51.810 --> 00:31:53.303
are not any longer.

00:31:54.640 --> 00:31:56.400
So now it was a different
time in which to dwell,

00:31:56.400 --> 00:31:59.963
for people, for fish
and for spirits as well.

00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:05.070
So as the story of the Lord
of the Fish, and the Naga,

00:32:05.070 --> 00:32:06.620
indicate the disappearance of fish,

00:32:06.620 --> 00:32:08.820
it's not just about economy,

00:32:08.820 --> 00:32:13.440
rather presents a fundamental
religious problem as well.

00:32:13.440 --> 00:32:15.810
Sources of invisible
potential on the river

00:32:15.810 --> 00:32:17.740
are not what they once were.

00:32:17.740 --> 00:32:20.160
Shrines to the Naga thought
to exist within the water,

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:23.200
were at times declared to
be shrines to dead Naga,

00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:24.730
where the spirits lived on,

00:32:24.730 --> 00:32:27.350
even after the physical
great serpents died,

00:32:27.350 --> 00:32:28.783
owing to the rivers change.

00:32:29.730 --> 00:32:33.050
As one fisherman told me
Nagas used to come out

00:32:33.050 --> 00:32:34.930
of the river, they would come into town,

00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:37.360
put on human clothing,
and come to the temple,

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:38.970
to listen to the Buddhist chanting.

00:32:38.970 --> 00:32:41.850
Sometimes they would even
marry women from the village,

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:43.660
and then they stopped.

00:32:43.660 --> 00:32:45.230
That's why I asked them to
press them a little bit further.

00:32:45.230 --> 00:32:46.909
Well, why did they stop?

00:32:46.909 --> 00:32:50.547
And he responded by simply,
"They got tired of us."

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:53.710
Elsewhere other river beings,

00:32:53.710 --> 00:32:55.900
underwent similar transformation.

00:32:55.900 --> 00:32:58.810
A Lao style medium, a very
similar religious professional

00:32:58.810 --> 00:33:03.420
who featured in the right
surrounding, the giant catfish

00:33:03.420 --> 00:33:06.470
a hundred years ago, was
the voice of an island King.

00:33:06.470 --> 00:33:07.880
A spirit that looked after the village,

00:33:07.880 --> 00:33:10.170
and set catches a fish to villagers nets.

00:33:10.170 --> 00:33:11.820
But found himself openly mocked,

00:33:11.820 --> 00:33:14.060
after a 2015 possession ritual,

00:33:14.060 --> 00:33:16.270
where as a new male Bangkok style medium

00:33:16.270 --> 00:33:18.620
who lived and set his life in a cave,

00:33:18.620 --> 00:33:20.810
behind the temple gained adherence.

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:23.500
Old orders based around
river and fish slip away,

00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:26.200
so replacement of the
representative of a new order,

00:33:26.200 --> 00:33:27.233
and a new flow.

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:29.433
Significantly here,

00:33:29.433 --> 00:33:31.780
the flows of international migrant labor,

00:33:31.780 --> 00:33:35.460
the struggle to get a good work contract,

00:33:35.460 --> 00:33:37.760
and to flow kind of
outwards from the village.

00:33:39.157 --> 00:33:40.450
It's the removal of religious figures

00:33:40.450 --> 00:33:42.830
from the physical realm,
including the realm of kinship,

00:33:42.830 --> 00:33:45.390
and participation in
communal religious activity

00:33:45.390 --> 00:33:48.880
also suggests a shift in
notions of materiality.

00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:51.300
The physical Naga, becomes a ghostly one.

00:33:51.300 --> 00:33:53.360
But it goes to the points
not to the uncanny,

00:33:53.360 --> 00:33:56.100
and not to haunting, but to
the presence of new promises,

00:33:56.100 --> 00:34:00.430
a new possibilities, even as
another way of being declines.

00:34:00.430 --> 00:34:02.590
It's a shift that occurs
as the workings of new

00:34:02.590 --> 00:34:06.510
liberal capitalism multiply,
as rubber prices rise and fall,

00:34:06.510 --> 00:34:08.320
as migrant labor becomes more tenuous,

00:34:08.320 --> 00:34:09.840
and as the political
future of the Northeast

00:34:09.840 --> 00:34:11.113
becomes more in depth.

00:34:11.970 --> 00:34:15.710
But more than this, the natural
world itself has changed.

00:34:15.710 --> 00:34:17.590
As the formerly predictable Mekong,

00:34:17.590 --> 00:34:20.490
full of beings with which one
had a particular relationship,

00:34:20.490 --> 00:34:22.840
becomes a new kind of a place.

00:34:22.840 --> 00:34:26.530
But, even as all that is
solid seems to melt into air,

00:34:26.530 --> 00:34:28.400
it does not disappear,

00:34:28.400 --> 00:34:31.180
As established economic and
environmental orders fail,

00:34:31.180 --> 00:34:34.250
and new miraculous or
catastrophic horizons

00:34:34.250 --> 00:34:37.823
of possibility open up, new
cosmological worlds are born.

00:34:39.160 --> 00:34:42.390
So, through a micro examination
of the impacts of Chinese,

00:34:42.390 --> 00:34:44.860
hydro-power on one
small fishing community.

00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:48.350
I wanna show the scale of such changes.

00:34:48.350 --> 00:34:51.050
The collapse of the Mekong
under new hydro-power projects,

00:34:51.050 --> 00:34:53.240
creates alterations
that can escape notice,

00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:55.500
if we only think about
the Mekong as a confluence

00:34:55.500 --> 00:34:59.170
of national interests, Bangkok,
Beijing, and Vientiane,

00:34:59.170 --> 00:35:01.580
might very well benefit
from the alterations

00:35:01.580 --> 00:35:03.240
taking place in the river.

00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:04.920
Thailand versus national interest

00:35:04.920 --> 00:35:05.896
and the capital in Bangkok,

00:35:05.896 --> 00:35:09.900
not necessarily in Isan
and Mekong regions.

00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:12.290
And Laos has is one of
its national priorities

00:35:12.290 --> 00:35:14.830
to become the battery of Asia.

00:35:14.830 --> 00:35:17.270
But for many that I discuss here,

00:35:17.270 --> 00:35:19.850
such changes involve multiple scales,

00:35:19.850 --> 00:35:21.820
including highly personal ones.

00:35:21.820 --> 00:35:25.630
The hydrology, the river
changes its color, its movement,

00:35:25.630 --> 00:35:28.130
even the way one Mark
space on the river change,

00:35:28.130 --> 00:35:31.143
this is a very intimate alteration.

00:35:32.470 --> 00:35:34.660
Ways of marking both space and time,

00:35:34.660 --> 00:35:37.720
ways of dividing territory,
dividing time or loss,

00:35:37.720 --> 00:35:39.970
ways of relating to other
inhabitants of the river,

00:35:39.970 --> 00:35:43.380
fish and spirits disappeared,
were to be replaced by

00:35:43.380 --> 00:35:46.130
instead described further
elsewhere, new hybrids,

00:35:46.130 --> 00:35:49.760
new spirits, new sources of
power, new sources of potential,

00:35:49.760 --> 00:35:51.380
ones that are more uncertain,

00:35:51.380 --> 00:35:53.050
and than ones that are more upfront.

00:35:53.050 --> 00:35:55.230
In short, as infrastructure itself alters

00:35:55.230 --> 00:35:58.215
the way the world works, new
sources of potential prosperous

00:35:58.215 --> 00:36:01.333
as well as disastrous become revealed.

00:36:02.800 --> 00:36:04.760
That's all I have for my talk right now.

00:36:04.760 --> 00:36:06.330
I would like ...

00:36:06.330 --> 00:36:10.430
If I could ask, like to show
a little bit more of the river

00:36:10.430 --> 00:36:11.273
as it is.

